OL,3,GNEWSAFamily urges PM to see social care
OL,4,Afirsthand
OL,5,
OL,6,FRelatives and care home bosses have
OL,7,Fwelcomed the prime minister's plan to
OL,8,Fchange the social care system - but
OL,9,Fcalled for quicker progress.
OL,11,FAndy Burnham has pledged to reform the
OL,12,Fadult social care system in England and
OL,13,Fmet Conservative and Liberal Democrat
OL,14,Fleaders to try to find "common ground".
OL,16,FCaroline May, whose mother-in-law Wendy
OL,17,Fis a Scarborough care home resident,
OL,18,Fcalled for care to be "free to us, with
OL,19,Four contributions" and urged Burnham to
OL,20,F"take a trip up to the Yorkshire coast
OL,21,Fand see firsthand what's happening".
OL,23,APub: 18-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,388,380,200,160,0,100
